# HuntDrafter-1 (lane HuntDrafter, 2026-10-30): a DFlash2 context update skips the launches whose ring rows the same
# update overwrites before it returns. The drafter's context is a ring of 2,176 rows (window 2,047 + block 8 + a tile)
# and a context update is row-wise (fc, norm, k / v projections, rotary; no attention), so in an update of R rows
# the rows i < R - 2,176 are overwritten by rows i + 2,176 of the same call and nothing can read them. A prompt chunk
# (TF_GLM_PREFILL_ROWS 4,096) commits its taps through MultiDrafter.commit in 64-row launches (t_max): 64 launches a
# chunk, of which the first 30 only write rows the last 34 overwrite. ring_skip() (dflash2.py, the one rule) drops
# those whole leading launches in MultiDrafter.commit (production's path: DraftContext.add_taps for every prompt
# chunk) and in the solo Drafter.add_taps (its 64-row pieces; pos_dev / context_end advanced past them); the launches
# left are the same rows in the same launches, so the same kernels, ring bits, device ends and context ends.
# Decode-round commits (a few rows a stream) are never wider than the ring and are untouched.
# Expected (GB10 taps graph at T=64 ~0.365 ms, DrafterFable's 0.382 minus 0108's 17 us): -30 launches = ~11 ms a
# 4,096-row chunk; cold ~200k (r1, 48 full chunks + 3,419) -1,459 launches ~ -0.53 s of 78.5 s (-0.7%); cold32
# -228 launches ~ -83 ms of 12.42 s (-0.7%); a warm +2.4k turn (r2) -3 launches ~ -1 ms. Every rank alike.
# Workstation RTX 5070 (test_ring_skip.py --bench, the test's small drafter): a 4,096-row chunk's update 11.68 -> 6.30
# ms (min of 20, median 19.6 -> 9.8).
# Exactness: test_ring_skip.py (the test_draft_pass_fusion.py harness: random DFlash2 checkpoint at world 3, the
# production 2,176-row ring, 4 streams): 70 single-stream chunks of 1 .. 8,197 rows at ends 0 .. 600,007 (ring edges)
# with every ring row of the pool, the device ends and context_end equal, multi-stream commits, block passes after
# the chunks, the solo drafter: ALL PASS on the patched tree; on the synced tree 49 FAIL (the launch counts).
--- tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/dflash2.py	2026-10-29 23:57:45.105314400 +0000
+++ tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/dflash2.py	2026-10-30 00:20:27.827331700 +0000
@@ -49,6 +49,16 @@
     return int(np.argmax(expect / ms))
 
 
+def ring_skip(rows: int, ring: int, step: int) -> int:
+    """Leading rows of a context update that need no launch: with a ring of ``ring`` rows (0: a flat buffer), a
+    row at offset i of an update of ``rows`` rows is overwritten by row i + ring of the same update when
+    i < rows - ring, before the update returns, so nothing can read it. Whole launches of ``step`` rows of such rows
+    are skipped; the launches left are the ones the update runs anyway, row for row (the same rows a launch, so the
+    same kernels and the same ring bits)."""
+
+    return max(0, (rows - ring) // step) * step if ring else 0
+
+
